{"id": "section-body-03452", "title": "Bacterial Cerebro-Spinal Meningitis", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Bacterial Infections", "Bacterial Cerebro-Spinal Meningitis"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-03452", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Bacterial Cerebro-Spinal Meningitis", "runs": [{"text": "Bacterial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Cerebro-Spinal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Meningitis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1802"}}, {"id": "body-03453", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Bacterial epidemics for Cerebro-Spinal Meningitis are commonly caused by Neisseria meningitidis. Other common bacteria are Haemophilus influenza, Staphylococcus aures and Streptococcus pneumoniae. Human-to-human disease transmission is via large respiratory droplets from the nose and throats of infected people. Incubation period is 2 to 10 days. Attack rates", "runs": [{"text": "Bacterial epidemics for Cerebro-Spinal Meningitis are commonly caused by Neisseria meningitidis. Other common bacteria are Haemophilus influenza, Staphylococcus aures and Streptococcus pneumoniae. Human-to-human disease transmission is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "via"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "large"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "respiratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "droplets"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "from"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "throats"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "people."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Incubation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "period"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "10"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "days."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Attack"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rates"}]}, {"id": "body-03455", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "are highest among children aged less than 15 years. Case fatality rates are usually 8-15% among treated patients, and >70% among untreated cases.", "runs": [{"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "highest"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "among"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "children"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "aged"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "less"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "than"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "15"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "years."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fatality"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rates"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8-15%"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "among"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": ">70% among untreated cases."}]}, {"id": "body-03457", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Case Definition", "runs": [{"text": "Case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Definition"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03458", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Suspected meningitis case: Any person with a sudden onset of fever (>38.5 °C rectal or 38.0 °C axillary), and neck stiffness or other meningeal signs and in case of infants, a bulging fontanelle.", "runs": [{"text": "Suspected meningitis case:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Any person with a sudden onset of fever (>38.5 °C rectal or 38.0 °C axillary), and neck stiffness or other meningeal signs and in case of infants, a bulging fontanelle."}]}, {"id": "body-03460", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Probable meningitis case: Any suspected case with macroscopic aspects of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) (turbid, cloudy or purulent); or with a CSF leukocyte count >10 cells/mm3 or with bacteria identified by Gram stain in CSF; or positive antigen detection (for example, by latex agglutination testing) in CSF", "runs": [{"text": "Probable meningitis case: Any suspected case with macroscopic aspects of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) (turbid, cloudy or purulent); or with a CSF leukocyte count >10 cells/mm3 or with bacteria identified by Gram stain in CSF; or positive antigen detection (for example, by latex agglutination testing) in CSF"}]}, {"id": "body-03462", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "In infants: CSF leucocyte count >100 cells/mm3; or CSF leucocyte count 10–100 cells/mm3 and either an elevated protein (>100 mg/dl) or decreased glucose (<40 mg/dl) level.", "runs": [{"text": "In infants: CSF leucocyte count >100 cells/mm3; or CSF leucocyte count 10–100 cells/mm3 and either an elevated protein (>100 mg/dl) or decreased glucose (<40 mg/dl) level."}]}, {"id": "body-03463", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Confirmed meningitis case: Any suspected or probable case that is laboratory confirmed by culturing or identifying (i.e. polymerase chain reaction) a bacterial pathogen (Neisseria meningitidis,", "runs": [{"text": "Confirmed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "meningitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Any"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "probable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laboratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "confirmed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "culturing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "identifying"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(i.e. polymerase chain reaction) a bacterial pathogen (Neisseria meningitidis,"}]}, {"id": "body-03464", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae type b) in the CSF or blood", "runs": [{"text": "Streptococcus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pneumoniae,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Haemophilus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenzae"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "type"